+\textbf{Source-to-Target Result and State Equivalence.}
+We randomly sampled 100 MySQL test cases and used the same cases to evaluate SQLGlot, RISE, \sedar{}, and \tool{} for transfer to DuckDB.
+We compared query results between the source and target executions for result equivalence, and compared the resulting database states, including schemas and table contents, for state equivalence.
+Translation or execution failures were counted as non-equivalent; both rates use all 100 test cases as the denominator.
+As shown in Table~\ref{tab:equivalence}, \tool{} achieves 52.0\% result equivalence and 74.0\% state equivalence, compared with 14.0\%/56.0\% for SQLGlot, 34.0\%/65.0\% for RISE, and 38.0\%/69.0\% for \sedar{}.
+These results provide supplementary evidence of behavioral preservation on the sampled MySQL-to-DuckDB cases, rather than a guarantee of semantic equivalence across dialects.
